  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bridge to Middle School</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Morocco):  The Bridge to Middle School activity will support the Ministry of Education (MOE) to identify strategies and alternatives for supporting students&apos; transition from upper primary to middle school. USAID will invest in the analysis and remediation of student learning difficulties in the upper primary grades, and in support of the development of innovative curricula and materials for grades 7-9 of the middle school instructional cycle. Provision of good quality curricula and improved instructional approaches will improve the knowledge and skills of the Moroccan population beyond present systems. USAID assistance will help build social and institutional capital, which will further advance Morocco on the path to self-reliance and will have a positive impact on the investment climate and sustainable inclusive growth.  The Bridge to Middle School activity will: a) analyze students&apos; difficulties in Arabic, science and math, in grades 4-6, b) assist the ministry to pilot innovative remediation strategies to address these challenges, c) support the development and piloting of new Arabic, English, and STEM curricula in grades 7-9, and d) conduct research and policy reform to facilitate the scale-up of these new curricula system-wide. This activity will generate data and information, which will further contribute to evidence-based policy development. Lessons learned from the pilot interventions will be used to support policy dialogue and the scale-up of national education reforms in upper-primary and middle schools.</narrative>
  </description>
